1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
 One side of the Terban bike path will be dismantled this winter.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,320
 It will be replaced by parking spots.

3
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:08,400
 This is the latest in a conversation that's been going on for years.

4
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:10,920
 So what do residents think about this?

5
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:14,820
 Let's hear from the warden of St. Monica's Parish, Paul Wong.

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,980
 It's right at the corner of Terban and Borden Street.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,300
 He's been a critic of the bike path.

8
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,760
 CBC's Dion Codrington caught up with him.

9
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:27,920
 There's been no daytime activities in the church basement since the bike path.

10
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:34,980
 And that has a lot to do with the fact that a lot of the daytime activities that went on in the church basement

11
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:39,500
 were mostly senior groups like bridge or various other activities.

12
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:46,480
 And a lot of them, they rely heavily on carpooling or even the setup of the bike path the way it was set up.

13
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:52,820
 So for walking, they had to park their cars a fair distance to come to the church.

14
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:55,080
 So it just wasn't worth their while anymore.

15
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:59,180
 And there has been a lot of accommodations thanks to the city on them.

16
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:05,920
 It's been like they have created like a driveway type dip in the sidewalk next to the church,

17
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:15,640
 which allows funerals to the hearse to back into there because the hearse were temporarily always blocking or stopping on Terban.

18
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:20,360
 So ultimately, what will this change mean for the church?

19
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,680
 Well, I think it's an improvement.

20
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:26,700
 Even the winter combination that I heard the city has been keeping us in the loop about,

21
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:36,900
 it is a good thing because in the winter, it is very tough for people to park their cars in front of the church or the thing

22
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,920
 because with the snow banks and everything like that.

23
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:46,640
 And I think the fact that if they free up one side of the road and allow people to park closer to the sidewalk,

24
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:50,060
 it will make the road in general a bit wider.

25
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:52,000
 And it's a temporary compromise.

26
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,980
 I mean, the cyclists have to understand that it's just for the winter.

27
00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:00,980
 However, not everyone happy with the borough's decision to close one of the separate bike lanes.

28
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:04,200
 Let's touch base now with NDG parent Anita Bertier.

29
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:04,960
 Good morning.

30
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:06,080
 Thanks for talking to us.

31
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,680
 Good morning, Sean.

32
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,740
 I'm happy to be here.

33
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:09,540
 Thanks for having me.

34
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:13,460
 Why are you opposing the closing of one side of the Terban bike path?

35
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:19,200
 Well, Sean, in about half an hour, I'll be making my way to school and work with my family.

36
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:24,320
 And we use it daily, just like many, many families within the borough.

37
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:32,880
 In fact, when we heard about this for the first time, some parents and I got together and we put together a petition

38
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:37,420
 and we went to schools and daycares where our children go.

39
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:44,060
 And we collected over 1,400 parent signatures just in just over a week.

40
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:50,600
 So, you know, people are very concerned that their day-to-day journey that they take,

41
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,500
 and that's their mode of transport, will not be safe anymore.

42
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:59,420
 So, you know, we just don't think that parking convenience and people's safety should carry equal weight.

43
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,380
 I don't think they do.

44
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:03,780
 And when you say that their daily commute won't be safe anymore, what do you mean by that?

45
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:10,840
 Well, if you look at the current configuration, there's two lanes, bike lanes on each side.

46
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:15,660
 So, we take the one all the way to school and that's the one that's going to be stripped away

47
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:19,140
 and there will now be a car parked on the bike lane.

48
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,560
 Then there will be a car moving on the actual road.

49
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:30,320
 And we are somehow expected to take our children in that tiny gap between a moving car and a parked car,

50
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:35,520
 which I just don't think any sort of safety expert is going to think is safe.

51
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,280
 And he said, do you use it in the winter as well?

52
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:39,600
 I do. We do use it.

53
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,300
 And that is the whole thing, Sean, is that if you think about the snow banks

54
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:49,160
 and the gentleman at the St. Monica's just mentioned that, you know, there are snow banks too.

55
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:52,840
 So, it's likely we will be cycling in the middle of the car lane.

56
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:59,100
 So, the whole idea of winning space and letting cars move freely is not going to happen anymore.

57
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:04,000
 I mean, I'm afraid the cars are going to be stuck behind me and my daughter as we cycle.

58
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,680
 And she's only seven, so she doesn't cycle very fast.

59
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:12,760
 My understanding though, and correct me if I'm wrong, that the cyclists would just all use that one side that's still open.

60
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:19,400
 No, Sean, that's not the case at all because each side of the cycle parts are actually very narrow.

61
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:25,320
 There's no way an engineer would be able to put two lanes within the one current lane.

62
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:29,880
 So, the idea is that the people going east will have to use the car lane.

63
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,540
 That's the whole thing.

64
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:36,000
 And, you know, the city says they're committed to Vision Zero by 2040.

65
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,940
 And that's, you know, to limit the number of deaths.

66
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,200
 And unfortunately, we've just had one last week.

67
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,400
 My heart goes out to that family.

68
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:48,960
 And I have to say that shocked us all when that happened because that could have been any of our teenagers.

69
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:53,440
 And that is under investigation that happened in Huntsick, Cartierville.

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,360
 Anita, this conversation has been going on for the better part of six years.

71
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,420
 How have you seen it evolved?

72
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:07,140
 Well, you know, we think it's a wonderful way to move into the future.

73
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:11,580
 And we do understand that when there's change, you know, people find that change very difficult.

74
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:18,620
 But when you're moving to the future, and we live on an island, so there is finite space for parking at the end of the day.

75
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:26,280
 You know, the fact we're trying to get people mobile and we're educating our children to be active and mobile and move around without cars.

76
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,580
 That is heading in the right direction.

77
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:34,400
 So, you know, this dismantlement does not seem to go in the future direction.

78
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,020
 It actually seems to be a step back.

79
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:43,200
 And what worries us, Sean, is that there seems to be a major incoherence right now between what the city mayor is saying.

80
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:47,820
 She's saying proactively in all the newspapers that she will not be dismantling.

81
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:52,060
 And then this is happening by decisions made in each borough.

82
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:55,040
 So, you know, something's not making sense here.

83
00:05:55,320 --> 00:06:11,720
 And our main safety concern at the moment is that in our borough, NDG, the city councilor of Loyola seems to be going through with a decision that is not based on any factual data or it's not based on any analysis yet.

84
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:15,200
 There is no safety expert has yet weighed in on this.

85
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:19,460
 So, we don't understand how this decision could go ahead.

86
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:26,100
 A couple of things I'll say about our conversation with Alexandra Tiedoresco, who is the city councilor for Loyola.

87
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,040
 He said a couple of things.

88
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,860
 We did get into conversation about parking.

89
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:33,220
 One of the things he said, it's not just about the number of available parking spaces.

90
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:36,220
 It's distance from destination as well.

91
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,220
 That might be an issue.

92
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:44,620
 Sure, there might be parking spaces a few blocks down the road, but then that means that person who might have to walk a bit.

93
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:46,220
 So, he brought that up as part of the conversation.

94
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:49,200
 But he also said that it's not going to be forever.

95
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,720
 This is going to be for the winter.

96
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:55,740
 And even the borough, when we asked for comment, they said that this is going to be for the winter.

97
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:00,180
 Well, we haven't seen that in writing, and we would love to see that in writing.

98
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:14,140
 I think that Councillor Emily Briere at the council meeting on Monday, and I have to say there were loads of families there, lots of small children with their helmets on, waiting patiently for their parents to watch the meeting and ask their questions.

99
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,180
 I think she summed it up the best.

100
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:22,180
 You know, she, at the end of the council meeting, she felt so moved, and she had listened to both parties.

101
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:33,720
 And she asked how the mayor could try to make such a decision using questionable data and zero analysis of the actual need for parking that is apparently at the heart of this decision.

102
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,120
 So, this is not a data-led, informed decision.

103
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,340
 There's no route plan.

104
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:42,300
 We haven't been showed anything about where we're supposed to cycle.

105
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:47,360
 There's no timeline that's been published, and there's no guarantee that the path will be reinstalled.

106
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:52,220
 Because if you think about it, Sean, you're going to uninstall it at a cost, which they don't know.

107
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:56,960
 They have no idea what the budget is for this, and they don't know how much it's going to cost.

108
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:07,540
 And my concern is that when it comes time in the spring to put it back, I think that the opposition might be saying, I mean, the people opposed to it might be saying, please don't spend more money putting it back.

109
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,080
 And then we'll go without.

110
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,600
 And we've fought so long for this, Sean.

111
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,980
 I've fought since my child is about one years old.

112
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,780
 I've been trying to get a safe bike path to go to the daycare.

113
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,580
 And she's seven now.

114
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:19,920
 Right.

115
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:23,100
 And again, we've been having this conversation for about that time as well.

116
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:29,100
 One of the other things that the Burroughs said, and Alexandra Tiedresco has said, Burroughs repeated it to us as well.

117
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:38,600
 The number of people, not many cyclists are using the Terrebonne bike path either side during the winter.

118
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:47,720
 Well, this is a very interesting one, because in the past 12 months, there's been 135,000 bike journeys.

119
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:53,480
 Now, that's 135,000 less car journeys along that two-kilometer stretch.

120
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:56,380
 And yes, of course, in winter, there is a drop.

121
00:08:56,380 --> 00:09:09,100
 But the statistics that the Loyola councillor gave were absolutely incorrect, because I think he chose one day during January in which there was an Environment Canada weather advisory.

122
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:14,500
 So that's definitely not representative of the clement weather that we've been having.

123
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:20,020
 And also during winter, my husband's a cyclist, it often just snows lightly and the path gets cleared.

124
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,400
 And it's actually great conditions for winter cyclists.

125
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:35,780
 So what I can tell you is that between December and March, the actual Burroughs' own bike counter on Avenue Kensington counts on average 40 to 60 cyclists a day along that bike path in the winter.

126
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:39,480
 And if you think about it, Sean, they're trying to win back 60 parkings.

127
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:44,580
 So, you know, you're just going to get those 60 cyclists now driving and looking for a parking.

128
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,400
 So that doesn't make sense to me.

129
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,320
 Compromise is a word that came up quite a bit.

130
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:51,840
 And again, in the statement from the borough, compromise is the word that came up quite a bit.

131
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:55,300
 Because, of course, again, we've been having this conversation for quite some time now.

132
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,740
 So compromise is one of the words that came out of this.

133
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:06,460
 And would this be a compromise, though, to address on one hand people who want to keep the bike path and on the other hand people who weren't so happy with it?

134
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:09,900
 You know, not in our opinion, Sean.

135
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:15,780
 And I mean, I don't think safety should ever be seen as a seasonal thing, especially when it comes to children.

136
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,900
 There's just no argument there.

137
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:26,620
 I just don't see how a parking could equate to my child's safety as she goes to school and putting her at risk and putting many families at risk.

138
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:35,300
 Over 1,000 families have said that they are scared and they're concerned and they won't be able to go to school anymore safely.

139
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:39,600
 And I think the Vision Zero commitments should be driving this.

140
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,300
 This should be behind their commitments.

141
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:47,240
 You know, at the end of the day, Sean, there were lots of children there at the council meeting.

142
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:58,920
 And what touched me the most was seeing drawings where they actually had put a line down the middle, some of them, and they put a car on one side and a bike or their scooter on the other side with them and their family.

143
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,060
 And they put a big heart in the middle.

144
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:04,340
 And I think that represents what children see here.

145
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:06,060
 They're like, let's share the road.

146
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,240
 Let's be happy.

147
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,260
 Let's share.

148
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:09,240
 Let's all be safe.

149
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,020
 And you know what?

150
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:22,460
 I really encourage residents that have parking, private parking within their property and driveways, of which there are over 60% of Taliban residents have parking, but they don't use it.

151
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:30,020
 So maybe they should chat to their neighbors, see if somebody needs the parking during the day, and they can put their car on their driveway or in their garage.

152
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,000
 Anita Bertier, we're going to leave it there for today.

153
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:36,340
 We'll continue this conversation with everyone who needs to be part of this conversation.

154
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,520
 But thank you this morning for your time.

155
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:40,660
 Thanks, Sean.

156
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:43,300
 And my little girl says a shout out to Lita Paulson.

157
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:46,660
 She really loves hearing her talk every day about the bike parts.

158
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,820
 And then a shout out right back at her.

159
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,600
 And there you go.

160
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,400
 Oh, thanks, Lita.

161
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:51,080
 Okay.

162
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,860
 That is Anita Bertier.

163
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:55,760
 Daybreak also reached out to the borough, as we said.

164
00:11:56,060 --> 00:12:05,240
 Mayor Stephanie Valenzuela told us she's working with experts to keep the bike lanes as it is for most of the year, and that her decision to keep only one lane open of the Taliban bike path is based on data.

165
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,300
 She says not many cyclists use it during the winter.

